  - title: "Hacking Browsers: The Easy Way"
    description: "When you think of hacking browsers, you perhaps think of V8 heap exploitation, deep-dive fuzzing, crazy sandbox escapes, and so on. But what if I told you that you can still find vulnerabilities in major browsers that don’t require any technical knowledge? Bugs you can even run into by accident!"
    speakers:
      - Robbe Van Roey / PinkDraconian
    start_utc: "2026-09-10T11:15:00Z"
    end_utc: "2026-09-10T12:00:00Z"
    tracks: 1
    room: ~
  - title: "45,724 Networks, One Flipper Zero: Mapping the Wireless Threat Landscape of Northern Ireland"
    description: Nearly one in ten WiFi networks across Northern Ireland is still advertising WPS - a protocol the Wi-Fi Alliance deprecated in 2012 due to well-documented cryptographic weaknesses. Most network owners have no idea.
    speakers:
      - M0r3al
    start_utc: "2026-09-10T10:30:00Z"
    end_utc: "2026-09-10T11:15:00Z"
    tracks: 1
    room: ~
  - title: "Bedtime Bug Hunting: A Friendly Android Auth Bypass Story"
    description: "One night, while lying in bed and idly poking around an Android app for a membership organisation I belong to, I found myself somewhere I did not expect to be: past the login flow."
    speakers:
      - Jeffrey Roe
    start_utc: "2026-09-10T14:40:00Z"
    end_utc: "2026-09-10T15:00:00Z"
    tracks: 2
    room: ~
  - title: QUICly Changing Network Comms
    description: "As defenses become more proactive and less reactive, the days of reliable unfettered egress to the internet are drawing to a close. At the same time, the increasing reliance on third parties necessitates increasing the size of the egress whitelist. The combination of the two requires a shift in C2 comms from relatively direct connections to infrastructure to proxying data via whitelisted services. Unfortunately, however, whitelisted services are often somewhat reluctant to get involved in even a simple shell-over-TLS connection, instead insisting on REST APIs, bespoke protocols, or worse."
    speakers:
      - Stuart McMurray
    start_utc: "2026-09-10T09:25:00Z"
    end_utc: "2026-09-10T10:10:00Z"
    tracks: 2
    room: ~
